cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Tensor Network-Based Machine Learning: Image Classification Benchmarks"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, YAML-driven pipeline for image classification with tensor
  networks, developed as a BSc Physics bachelor's thesis (TFG). It provides a
  reference Matrix Product State (MPS) baseline built on TensorKrowch, a custom
  hierarchical Tree Tensor Network (TTN), a hybrid TTN that interleaves PyTorch
  transformations between tensor-network levels, and an AIM spatial front-end
  inspired by the Deep Tree Tensor Network paper. The models are compared under
  identical data and training conditions on the ChemEq25 chemistry lab apparatus
  dataset, reformulated from object detection into instance classification by
  cropping annotated objects, with Oxford Flowers 102 kept as a preliminary
  benchmark.
